00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.465
Now, our cat function isn't very smart.

00:00:03.465 --> 00:00:06.810
It makes the same cat every single time.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:10.540
I'm going to factor it a bit so we can make all kinds of cats.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.490
Now, right now, when you call it to make a new cat,

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.520
it just runs this function and does all of this stuff.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.200
But we're not passing anything into it.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.040
Let's pass an object literal into our cat constructor function.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.690
I'm gonna call it data.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.055
Now, if someone gave us, say,

00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:28.950
an array of cat data,

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.695
we can easily make those different cats.

00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:33.330
By saying new cat,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.295
and passing an object literal.

00:00:35.295 --> 00:00:37.485
See, thinking ahead is good.

00:00:37.485 --> 00:00:40.020
Now, let's go through the steps to make this work.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.780
Now before we tackle this part here,

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.790
let's tackle what gets passed in.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.400
Down here when I say new cat,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.725
I'm going to pass in that object literal.

00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:52.200
Later on, we'll actually have multiple cats,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.265
so we'll be doing this again and again and again for each cat object.

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:59.340
Now, here are the various properties for the same cat

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.610
that our cat function up above was making over and over again.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.420
Now, we're passing them into the Cat Constructor Function.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.440
Now up at the top,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.710
instead of actually setting these values like this,

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.085
we're going to actually set them based on the data that gets passed in.

00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:19.605
So, this dot click count will actually be equal to data.click count.

00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:23.625
From the object literal that we pass down below into here,

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:27.330
we'll set the click count of that to the cat we're creating.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.850
We'll do the same thing for all the rest of them.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.225
Now this dot title stays exactly the same,

00:01:33.225 --> 00:01:34.800
because for every cat,

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.435
if the clicks are less than 10,

00:01:36.435 --> 00:01:38.115
the title will be newborn.

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:40.755
Less than 50 is infant, et cetera.

00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:43.065
That's hard coded into the cat.

00:01:43.065 --> 00:01:48.000
Now rather than having our data actually explicitly set here,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.780
we're setting the data down here where we create these cats.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.640
Now we're ready for more cats,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.960
let's add them in the next video.

